{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DRUPAL-CONTRIB-2026-304","published":"2026-11-04T17:34:29Z","modified":"2026-11-04T20:30:03.729981467Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-122073"],"details":"The Name Field module provides a field for storing a personal name as separate components.\n\nThe module does not sufficiently sanitize values under some circumstances. A name stored on the field can be interpreted as HTML, which can lead to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"drupal/name","ecosystem":"Packagist:https://packages.drupal.org/8","purl":"pkg:composer/drupal/name?repository_url=https:%2F%2Fpackages.drupal.org%2F8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.6.0"}],"database_specific":{"constraint":"<1.6.0"}}],"database_specific":{"affected_versions":"<1.6.0","source":"https://github.com/DrupalSecurityTeam/drupal-advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/name/DRUPAL-CONTRIB-2026-304.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.drupal.org/sa-contrib-2026-304"}],"credits":[{"name":"Conrad Lara (cmlara)","contact":["https://www.drupal.org/u/cmlara"]}]}